{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgF8p4TsouFxBJULUMeQA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"prompt\": \"A square abstract painting filling the entire canvas edge to edge, with no frame, border, wall, room, or gallery setting. Nonrepresentational throughout: no recognizable objects, figures, faces, bodies, scenes, landscapes, horizons, machines, diagrams, symbols, icons, letters, numbers, or text. Palette: a deep indigo-black ground with a band of cool teal running diagonally through it, interrupted by a warm ochre-orange mass that pushes forward from the lower left. Small flares of vermilion and pale ivory sit near the center as points of high contrast. Brushwork varies sharply: dense, scraped, palette-knife impasto in the orange area, thin translucent glazes layered over the teal, and fast dry-brush strokes at the edges that leave the ground showing through. Gesture should feel both controlled and urgent, with a few long, deliberate sweeps crossing several sssharp, jittery marks. Texture ranges from smooth, varnish-like patches to crusted, granular passages. Layering: at least four visible strata, with some translucent layers and some opaque overpaints that partially cover earlier marks. Rhythm comes from repeated short parallel strokes on the right side that gradually slow and spread into open space. Spatial tension: the ochre mass presses against the teal diagonal, and a thin pale line of paint seems to hold the two apart. Leave generous areas of empty ground in the upper right and bottom center so the density feels deliberate rather than uniform. Overall mood: restless, weighed, and exact, with no single focal point resolved.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":435,"cache_read_input_tokens":16315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":435},"output_tok